WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.960
Welcome to the Teacher Training Tracker.

2
00:00:02.960 --> 00:00:09.769
We’ll take a closer look at the main modules using the Admin, Trainer, and Trainee journeys.

3
00:00:09.769 --> 00:00:22.424
On the Admin dashboard, programme health is brought together through school readiness, teacher and student batches, trainer availability, timeline, and progress summaries.

4
00:00:22.424 --> 00:00:26.790
The figures in this prototype are illustrative sample data.

5
00:00:27.190 --> 00:00:32.169
The Project module keeps the programme scope and key dates visible.

6
00:00:32.169 --> 00:00:41.607
Training plans turn that scope into five teacher phases, totalling twenty-five hours, and a student programme of fifteen hours.

7
00:00:41.607 --> 00:00:52.160
Day-wise activities, learning resources, assessment, and feedback can be reviewed together, so the plan is clear before batches are scheduled.

8
00:00:52.560 --> 00:00:59.749
The Batch Upload module accepts a schedule file and shows validation feedback before import.

9
00:00:59.749 --> 00:01:07.484
Admins can review batch details alongside trainer availability and resolve coverage concerns early.

10
00:01:07.484 --> 00:01:15.220
This connects school readiness, the training plan, dates, and the trainer responsible for delivery.

11
00:01:15.620 --> 00:01:27.492
The reporting area brings together programme summary, school readiness and coverage, batch performance, attendance, trainer availability, and resource usage.

12
00:01:27.492 --> 00:01:32.710
Filters help narrow a view by state, dates, training plan, or status.

13
00:01:32.710 --> 00:01:41.330
Each report is designed to help teams move from a programme-level question to the relevant batch or school detail.

14
00:01:41.730 --> 00:01:47.976
In the Trainer workspace, My Work highlights assigned batches and upcoming sessions.

15
00:01:47.976 --> 00:01:57.345
Trainers can open participant registration, the day-wise training plan, and the content library from the same role-based menu.

16
00:01:57.345 --> 00:02:02.550
This keeps the practical steps for preparing a session close together.

17
00:02:02.950 --> 00:02:10.204
The participant module shows registrations, approval status, capacity, and the assigned batch.

18
00:02:10.204 --> 00:02:15.220
Trainers can review the final list before the first training day.

19
00:02:15.220 --> 00:02:25.330
In Mark Attendance, they select the session date and record each approved participant as present or absent, then save the register.

20
00:02:25.730 --> 00:02:31.256
The Content Library connects resources to the training plan and audience.

21
00:02:31.256 --> 00:02:40.642
It includes sample PDFs, video previews, presentations, interactive learning packages, and forms for assessment or feedback.

22
00:02:40.642 --> 00:02:48.590
In this prototype, the previews are interactive and saved form submissions remain in the current browser.

23
00:02:48.990 --> 00:02:58.109
The Trainee view, called My Training, shows phase progress, the next session, day-wise activities, and the resources for learning.

24
00:02:58.109 --> 00:03:08.560
A learner can see which phase is under way and what comes next, so the programme feels like a guided journey rather than a list of separate sessions.

25
00:03:08.960 --> 00:03:16.368
The Assessment module presents pre-training and post-training questions at the relevant point in a phase.

26
00:03:16.368 --> 00:03:20.954
Session Feedback collects a short rating and an optional comment.

27
00:03:20.954 --> 00:03:31.890
The Certificates view shows progress toward initial and full-programme certificates; the completion criteria shown here are placeholders in this prototype.

28
00:03:32.290 --> 00:03:39.357
Together, these modules connect programme oversight, session delivery, and learner progress.

29
00:03:39.357 --> 00:03:49.727
This is a browser-based prototype using sample data; its sign-in is for demonstration, and some changes are stored only in the browser.

30
00:03:49.727 --> 00:03:51.494
Thank you for watching.

31
00:03:51.494 --> 00:03:56.180
Which module would you like to explore in a live walkthrough?
